       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter sertraline 1000 mg daily, even with your confirmation. I have no way to verify the clinical rationale, and 1000 mg is five times the labeled maximum of 200 mg per day. At that dose, serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity are real risks.\n\nYou have a few options:\n- **Dose within the labeled range:** Give me a dose of 200 mg/day or less, and I'll enter it right away. For example, 50 mg, 100 mg, or 200 mg by mouth once daily.\n- **Dose above the labeled maximum:** This needs to go through your pharmacy and the prescriber of record, following your institution's process for off-label or above-maximum dosing. That usually means a pharmacist review and documented approval, and it may involve psychiatry or toxicology. The order can be entered once that process is complete and the dose is handled outside my safeguards.\n- **Possible error:** If 1000 mg came from a typo or a unit mix-up, tell me the correct dose.\n\nI'm glad to enter a dose within the labeled range now."
      }
